  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A faded composite of the Stable Diffusion variations with new black line drawing starting over the lower right slope, rocks and a tree.",
    "description": "A square screenshot of the drawing in progress. The variations are stacked as semi transparent layers, so the lake, mountains, the red roofed house, flat topped trees and waterfall from variation 3 show through as a pale wash, with houses from variation 1 ghosted at left. Over this, crisp black outlines have been drawn across the bottom third and the right side: rocky ledges, boulders, clumps of rounded shrubs, a tall pine at left, a stream at bottom right and a bushy tree at the right edge. The new line work has only light colour from the layers beneath.",
    "impression": "The moment the hand takes over. The generated scenes become tracing paper, and the drawing borrows from several of them at once, picking a house here and a rock there. You can see how the pale reference and the confident new line belong to different worlds.",
